# runtime / build / cache (machine-local)
.tests/
# Bare `node_modules` (no trailing slash) matches a directory AND a symlink, at
# any depth. The slash form matches directories only — which is how six
# self-referential `super-dsh/agent-*/node_modules` symlinks got committed in
# 0ff0322 (2026-09-26) and then let every checkout clobber the real installs.
node_modules
# Same trap for the vendored checkout: the main repo holds a real directory
# while a `.worktrees/*` checkout carries a symlink into it, so a trailing
# slash silently exempted the symlink form. A bare `/upstream` matches both,
# and `upstream` must never be a repo artifact at all.
/upstream
.dsh_better_edit/
.npm-cache/

